WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.397
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Monday, November second.

2
00:00:04.397 --> 00:00:07.272
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.272 --> 00:00:11.942
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:11.942 --> 00:00:13.518
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:13.518 --> 00:00:20.155
Two more vessels were struck in Gulf waters on Sunday, one in the Strait of Hormuz and one off Saudi Arabia.

6
00:00:20.155 --> 00:00:26.768
A severe cyclone is forecast to reach India's Andhra Pradesh coast tonight, a week after Cyclone Arnab.

7
00:00:26.768 --> 00:00:32.711
And a power failure cut electricity across northern Peru on Sunday afternoon.

8
00:00:32.711 --> 00:00:33.849
Here's the detail.

9
00:00:33.849 --> 00:00:36.882
Gulf shipping.

10
00:00:36.882 --> 00:00:45.566
Confirmed by UK Maritime Trade Operations: on Sunday afternoon, a ship's master relayed a Mayday reporting that another vessel had been struck by an unknown projectile in the Strait of Hormuz.

11
00:00:45.566 --> 00:00:55.096
Reported, per a maritime security firm quoted in trade press: the vessel was a tug, and it was partially sinking.

12
00:00:55.096 --> 00:00:56.059
UKMTO has not named it.

13
00:00:56.059 --> 00:01:04.705
Overnight, UKMTO says a tanker was hit by two projectiles in the Arabian Gulf, about seventy-two nautical miles off the Saudi coast near Kuwait.

14
00:01:04.705 --> 00:01:09.055
All crew are accounted for, and no environmental impact was reported.

15
00:01:09.055 --> 00:01:20.654
Separately, Iran's Revolutionary Guard navy said, via Iranian state media, that two oil tankers exploded after hitting mines on what it called an unauthorized route through the strait.

16
00:01:20.654 --> 00:01:22.367
It named no vessels.

17
00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:28.747
That is a claim only, with no independent confirmation, and not matched to the UKMTO reports.

18
00:01:28.747 --> 00:01:35.298
The latest joint maritime threat update, issued before both incidents, rates the Strait of Hormuz severe, and the Arabian Gulf substantial.

19
00:01:35.298 --> 00:01:46.155
Tueri suggests operators with Gulf voyages review routing and reporting procedures against that assessment, and treat the mine claim as unverified, not dismissed.

20
00:01:46.155 --> 00:01:47.441
India.

21
00:01:47.441 --> 00:01:56.668
Confirmed by the India Meteorological Department: Severe Cyclonic Storm Murasu is forecast to cross the south Andhra Pradesh coast between about eleven thirty tonight and four a.m.

22
00:01:56.668 --> 00:02:04.702
Tuesday, India time, with winds of one hundred to one hundred ten kilometers per hour, gusting to one hundred twenty.

23
00:02:04.702 --> 00:02:11.714
It has issued a red message for Andhra Pradesh and nearby north Tamil Nadu coasts.

24
00:02:11.714 --> 00:02:13.138
That is a forecast, not an observed landfall.

25
00:02:13.138 --> 00:02:22.436
Reported, per a state disaster official quoted by Reuters: about two thousand people have been evacuated in Andhra Pradesh, with plans to move about thirty thousand.

26
00:02:22.436 --> 00:02:35.875
Tueri suggests organizations with people in coastal Andhra Pradesh confirm shelter plans and contact procedures before nightfall, and expect road and power disruption on Tuesday.

27
00:02:35.875 --> 00:02:36.846
Peru.

28
00:02:36.846 --> 00:02:47.907
Reported, per power companies quoted in local media: a grid fault at about three p.m. local time on Sunday, linked in preliminary reports to a high-voltage line near Trujillo, cut power across northern regions including Tumbes and Piura.

29
00:02:47.907 --> 00:02:56.488
One distributor reported about six hundred eighteen thousand customers affected.

30
00:02:56.488 --> 00:03:04.347
Cloudflare's internet measurements show traffic in Tumbes fell to near zero, and was recovering by about a quarter to six local time.

31
00:03:04.347 --> 00:03:06.909
Restoration is reported by operators; we have not confirmed it for end users.

32
00:03:06.909 --> 00:03:12.046
The grid operator has not published a cause.

33
00:03:12.046 --> 00:03:13.511
Operations check.

34
00:03:13.511 --> 00:03:21.976
Aviation: at about two forty p.m. local time today, Flightradar twenty-four showed about twenty-seven percent of Riyadh flights cancelled.

35
00:03:21.976 --> 00:03:26.919
That figure is counted on a different base from Sunday's, so no trend can be drawn.

36
00:03:26.919 --> 00:03:38.869
Security: the Saudi-led coalition said it intercepted a ballistic missile and a drone aimed at southern Saudi Arabia on Sunday; Reported: the coalition says it intercepted another missile today.

37
00:03:38.869 --> 00:03:48.448
Maritime: we found no new statement from Iran's Hormuz authority on action against vessels linked to a South Korean shipping group; that remains a claim only.

38
00:03:48.448 --> 00:03:57.142
Borders and health: the US Ebola attestation rule for all flights to the United States applies from eleven fifty-nine p.m.

39
00:03:57.142 --> 00:03:58.284
Eastern on Tuesday, unchanged.

40
00:03:58.284 --> 00:04:03.345
Galapagos: Britain's Foreign Office updated its flooding advice again on Sunday.

41
00:04:03.345 --> 00:04:09.614
Reported: Baltra airport is operating, but piped water in Puerto Ayora is still suspended.

42
00:04:09.614 --> 00:04:15.441
Infrastructure, reported: drone strikes hit two power substations in eastern Sudan today, causing wide outages.

43
00:04:15.441 --> 00:04:18.037
Hazards: Mayon volcano in the Philippines stays at alert level three.

44
00:04:18.037 --> 00:04:29.620
Ground transport: Spain's Madrid to Andalusia high-speed line remains suspended; a mid-November reopening is reported, not confirmed by the operator.

45
00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.683
That's today's brief.

46
00:04:31.683 --> 00:04:33.162
Current as of six a.m.

47
00:04:33.162 --> 00:04:33.925
Central, Monday.

48
00:04:33.925 --> 00:04:35.973
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

49
00:04:35.973 --> 00:04:40.932
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

50
00:04:40.932 --> 00:04:42.996
Check the original source before you act.

51
00:04:42.996 --> 00:04:54.477
Tueri Systems provides information verification, communications support, and operational decision support for organizations working in changing conditions.

52
00:04:54.477 --> 00:04:57.190
Learn more at tuerisystems.com.

53
00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.268
Thanks for listening.
